{"id":"u-acefdf3f-cdb2-4650-8402-c9645b0d496e","src":"community","title":"Return to Moria","author":"Ömer Taha Arslan","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/C8z1x1-home-gym","desc":"WEEKLY SCHEDULE\n\nDays 1, 2, 3: Full-body strength/hypertrophy (Mon/Wed/Fri)\nDay 4 (Optional): Conditioning circuit (Sat/Sun)\nRest: 3-4 days per week\n\nStart with Day 4 as written for 4 weeks. Track how you feel:\nIf you're recovering well and progressing on Days 1-3 → keep it\nIf you're constantly tired or lifts stalling → swap to light cardio or skip\nIf you love it → add more conditioning work\nIf you hate it → replace with active hobby (sports, hiking, etc.)\n\nWEEKLY VOLUME\n\nEach muscle: 10-16 sets/week\nFrequency: Every muscle 3x/week (optimal for growth)\nTotal workout time: 50-70 min per session\n\n\nPROGRESSION STRATEGY\nPrimary Method: Add Reps First\nWeeks 1-3:\n\nPick a rep range (e.g., 6-8 reps)\nWhen you hit top of range on ALL sets → add 1-2 reps next session\nWhen you exceed range (hitting 9-10 reps) → increase weight\n\nExample:\n\nWeek 1: Squat 80kg x 6,6,6,5 reps\nWeek 2: Squat 80kg x 7,7,6,6 reps\nWeek 3: Squat 80kg x 8,8,8,7 reps\nWeek 4: Squat 82.5kg x 6,6,5,5 reps (increase weight, drop reps)\n\nWeight Increases\n\nUpper body exercises: +1.25-2.5kg\nLower body exercises: +2.5-5kg\nOnly increase when hitting top rep range for 2 consecutive weeks\n\nDeload Week (Every 6-8 Weeks)\n\nReduce weight to 60% of working weight\nKeep same reps/sets\nAllows nervous system recovery\nPrevents injury and burnout","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-06-14T15:07:17.280Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulde